M1 APPLIES: plan: the salt fetched per hash (nothing kept or held)
M2 APPLIES: plan: the reference hashed without the bank code
M3 APPLIES: plan: keychainAccessible omitted
M4 APPLIES: plan: the account update sent without a command
R1 APPLIES: the batch sent as a JSON body (parsed by the dispatcher at 2 MiB; the route gets no stream)
R2 APPLIES: the batch's bytes typed application/json
R3 APPLIES: the read waits the transport's 20 s
R4 APPLIES: the read is a command, so the transport resends it
R5 APPLIES: any salt answer
R6 APPLIES: any batch answer
R7 APPLIES: any drafts page
R8 APPLIES: a later page without its limit
R9 APPLIES: a later page without its cursor
R10 APPLIES: an ack for another entity
R11 APPLIES: an ack for another command
R12 APPLIES: confirm without its command
R13 APPLIES: dismiss without its command
R14 APPLIES: dismiss without a body
R15 APPLIES: a draft id that is no UUID is sent
R16 APPLIES: an account id that is no UUID is sent
R17 APPLIES: the account update without If-Match
R18 APPLIES: the account update's command id is the account's
R19 APPLIES: another account's answer accepted
R20 APPLIES: any accounts answer
R21 APPLIES: any 204 answer
R22 APPLIES: any albums answer
R23 APPLIES: the device registered with POST
R24 APPLIES: the update's default id is not expo-crypto's
H1 APPLIES: keychainAccessible WHEN_UNLOCKED (an iCloud backup may restore it to another device)
H2 APPLIES: the access group ignored
H3 APPLIES: another key prefix
H4 APPLIES: a kept value read without its check
H5 APPLIES: the read without its options
H6 APPLIES: the write without its options
H7 APPLIES: forget deletes nothing
H8 APPLIES: forget without its options
H9 APPLIES: an unnormalizable reference is hashed
H10 APPLIES: a failed salt load is kept, so it fails for good
H11 APPLIES: the kept salt ignored
H12 APPLIES: the fetched salt not kept
H13 APPLIES: a locked keychain falls back to the server
H14 APPLIES: base64url read as base64
H15 APPLIES: hex without leading zeros
H16 APPLIES: SHA-512 for SHA-256
F1 APPLIES: slip import closed is ignored
F2 APPLIES: the salt behind the release
F3 APPLIES: slip refs behind the release
F4 APPLIES: a confirm naming a gone draft is accepted
F5 APPLIES: a dismiss of a gone draft is accepted
F6 APPLIES: confirm takes nothing out
F7 APPLIES: a stale account update is accepted
F8 APPLIES: an unknown account is updated
F9 APPLIES: an update keeps the version
F10 APPLIES: pages ignore the limit
F11 APPLIES: an unscripted slip is read
F12 APPLIES: the fake salt is not a salt
F13 APPLIES: calls are not recorded
D1 APPLIES: the erase forgets no slip salt
D2 APPLIES: a keychain that refuses stops the erase
D3 APPLIES: the web's erase reaches the keychain
V1 APPLIES: slip calls over a transport without the analytics header
V2 APPLIES: a new slip client per call
T1 APPLIES: a link to a route that does not exist
T2 APPLIES: the manual run's link to a route that does not exist
